  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">India - Fiber-to-the-home equipment</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In order to scale up additional funding from DGGF has been granted in order to expand the current assembly facility and setup a new Photonics production facility in India.

In 2021 DGGF supplied a guarantee to the loan of the Indian bank so that GX International BV (GX) will be able to expand their activities in the production of fiber optic equipment. GX is a Dutch company active in India in the production of hardware/software for Fiber to the home (FTTH) connections. In other words, GX provides the hardware and software to connect homes to fiber optic networks of telecom operators. GX has traditionally been active in India and sees the demand for its services increasing due to the Corona. In order to respond to this demand or to meet this demand, GX needs additional working capital. Furthermore in the near future an investment will be made to set up a production facility. Update 2022: With an additional DGGF finance of EUR2mln GX will be able to expand their current assembly facility to deal with increase in demand, further integrate backwards into the manufacturing process, install solar-panels, and preparation of a new R&amp;D facility.</narrative>
  </description>
